<!--
  Entitlements for the notarised release (hardened runtime, no App Sandbox).

  Virtual Serial Studio asks for no exception to the hardened runtime: it does
  not generate code at run time (no JIT, no unsigned executable memory), it loads
  only libraries and plug-ins that are signed with the same identity in the
  bundle, and it has no use for the camera, microphone, contacts or location.
  Serial devices (/dev/cu.*) are plain files that need no entitlement outside the
  sandbox, and incoming connections are the Application Firewall's business, not
  an entitlement. The dictionary is empty on purpose; do not add a key without a
  reason written next to it. A sandboxed build uses vss_gui.sandbox.entitlements.
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict/>
</plist>
